#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0387 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Row 1's RPATHCD is empty -> FIRES; row 2 populates it. M3-D22 corrected the metadata rather than the Check: the Description said RPATHCD 'should be populated when Reproductive Paths have been defined in the Trial Repro Paths (TP) dataset' and the Executability said 'Partially Executable - Possible Overreporting', but sheet rows 1894-1895 carry an EMPTY Condition cell, a flatly unconditional Plain Text ('RPATHCD must be populated in DM') and Rule 'DM.RPATHCD ^= null'. Since the sheet states no condition, nothing is under-implemented and there is nothing to over-report; the Check was already right and is UNCHANGED. The TP block is present so the fixture is valid under a hypothetical TP-gated reading too."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=S1-001
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col SPECIES type=Char label="Species"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col RPATHCD type=Char label="Reproductive Path Code"
col SETCD   type=Char label="Set Code"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | 001 | RAT | F | HD |    | SET1
S1 | DM | S1-002 | 002 | RAT | F | HD | P1 | SET1
---

dataset TP label="Trial Repro Paths"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col RPATHCD type=Char label="Reproductive Path Code"
col RPATH   type=Char label="Reproductive Path"
col RPRFDY  type=Num  label="Planned Repro Phase Day of First Exposure"
---
S1 | TP | P1 | F0 Female | 0
---
